WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:01.548
Hi there!

2
00:00:01.549 --> 00:00:04.000
Who are

3
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.876
you? I'm a

4
00:00:06.876 --> 00:00:09.825
moose. Moose are

5
00:00:09.825 --> 00:00:15.203
the biggest kind of deer. Where do

6
00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:17.419
you live? Moose live

7
00:00:17.419 --> 00:00:21.425
in cold parts of the world. We like

8
00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:24.362
forests. We stay

9
00:00:24.362 --> 00:00:30.014
near lakes, ponds, or streams. Can

10
00:00:30.014 --> 00:00:32.281
you swim? Yes,

11
00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:36.359
we're great swimmers. We

12
00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:41.147
can also run fast. It's

13
00:00:41.147 --> 00:00:43.814
cold here! Moose

14
00:00:43.814 --> 00:00:47.411
love the cold. Our

15
00:00:47.411 --> 00:00:50.946
fur keeps us warm. Our

16
00:00:50.947 --> 00:00:56.334
hooves help us walk in snow. What

17
00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:59.280
do you eat? Moose

18
00:00:59.281 --> 00:01:02.113
don't eat meat. We

19
00:01:02.114 --> 00:01:07.977
eat twigs, bark, leaves, and pinecones. We

20
00:01:07.977 --> 00:01:12.749
also eat plants that grow in water. You

21
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.168
have big antlers! My

22
00:01:16.168 --> 00:01:19.864
antlers fall off each year. Then

23
00:01:19.864 --> 00:01:23.902
they grow back—even bigger. We

24
00:01:23.902 --> 00:01:29.058
use antlers to find mates and fight.

25
00:01:29.058 --> 00:01:31.500
Who do you fight?

26
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.594
Male moose fight each other.

27
00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:38.544
We also fight enemies.

28
00:01:38.544 --> 00:01:46.113
Bears, wolves, and cougars hunt us.

29
00:01:46.113 --> 00:01:49.097
I'm going for a swim now.

30
00:01:49.097 --> 00:01:52.709
I'll see you later.

31
00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:58.874
Good-bye, Moose!

